SLUG: services/intercity-relocation.html
TITLE: Intercity Relocation from Kanpur — long-distance moving
DESC: City-to-city household relocation from Kanpur in a dedicated vehicle, with the driver's contact shared at dispatch and a delivery window agreed before departure.
HEADING: Intercity &amp; long-distance moving
LEAD: City-to-city relocation in a dedicated vehicle, with a delivery window agreed before it leaves and updates along the way.
CRUMBS: Home|/ ; Services|/services.html ; Intercity relocation|
---

  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split is-wide-left">
        <div>
          <h2>Dedicated vehicle or shared load</h2>
          <p class="lead">
            This is the single biggest choice on an intercity move, and it is
            worth understanding before you compare quotes — because two quotes
            that look different are often quoting different things.
          </p>
          <p>
            A <strong>dedicated vehicle</strong> carries only your goods. It
            leaves when you are ready and drives to your destination, so the
            timeline is predictable and nothing is handled in between. This is
            our default.
          </p>
          <p>
            A <strong>shared part-load</strong> puts your goods on a vehicle
            with other consignments going the same way. It costs less, and it
            is a perfectly sensible choice for a small inventory on a flexible
            date — but delivery depends on the other consignments, so the
            window is wider and your goods are handled more.
          </p>
          <p>
            We will quote whichever suits you, and we will say which one we
            would choose for your inventory.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <span class="card__icon"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-route"/></svg></span>
          <h3>Included as standard</h3>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Dedicated vehicle unless you choose a shared load</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Packing rated for long-distance vibration, not just handling</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Load strapped in sections and checked before departure</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Driver's contact shared with you at dispatch</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Delivery window agreed in writing before the vehicle leaves</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Progress updates on WhatsApp</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section on-sunk">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Being straight about it</span>
        <h2>What we will and will not promise</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>We commit to a delivery window</h3>
          <p>
            Agreed before the vehicle leaves and kept updated as it travels.
            If it slips, you hear it from us before you have to ask.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>We will not promise an exact hour</h3>
          <p>
            Several hundred kilometres out, nobody can honour that. Any mover
            who gives you a precise arrival time for a long route is guessing,
            and the guess is what you will argue about later.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Packing matters more over distance</h3>
          <p>
            A carton that survives a cross-town trip can still fail over eight
            hundred kilometres of road vibration. Long-distance loads are
            packed with more fill and fewer part-empty cartons.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Ask every mover about transit cover</h3>
          <p>
            Goods are not automatically insured in transit, with us or anyone
            else. Ask what cover is included, what it excludes, and get it in
            writing with the quote.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <h2>What changes the price</h2>
          <ol class="steps mt-6">
            <li class="step"><div>
              <h3>Distance</h3>
              <p>The obvious one, though it is not linear — a return leg with no load back affects the rate.</p>
            </div></li>
            <li class="step"><div>
              <h3>Vehicle size</h3>
              <p>Set by your inventory. Under-sizing to win a quote is how a second trip appears later.</p>
            </div></li>
            <li class="step"><div>
              <h3>Dedicated or shared</h3>
              <p>A shared part-load costs less and delivers in a wider window.</p>
            </div></li>
            <li class="step"><div>
              <h3>Access at both ends</h3>
              <p>Still applies. A long carry in a new city costs the same as one at home.</p>
            </div></li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>Questions we get asked</h2>
          <div class="faq mt-6" data-faq>
            <details>
              <summary>How long will it take to arrive?</summary>
              <div class="faq__body"><p>
                It depends on the route and whether the load is dedicated or
                shared. We give you a window in writing before the vehicle
                leaves, based on that specific route, rather than a generic
                figure.
              </p></div>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>Can I track the vehicle?</summary>
              <div class="faq__body"><p>
                You get the driver's number at dispatch and progress updates
                from your coordinator on WhatsApp. If live GPS tracking is
                available on the vehicle assigned to you, we will tell you at
                booking rather than implying every vehicle has it.
              </p></div>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>Can my car go on the same booking?</summary>
              <div class="faq__body"><p>
                Yes. Vehicle transport runs in a covered carrier and can be
                coordinated with your household goods so both arrive around
                the same time. See
                <a href="/services/vehicle-transport.html">car and bike transport</a>.
              </p></div>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>What if my new home is not ready when it arrives?</summary>
              <div class="faq__body"><p>
                Tell us as early as you can and we will hold the consignment in
                <a href="/services/storage-warehousing.html">storage</a> and
                deliver when you are ready. Arranged in advance it costs
                noticeably less than arranging it on the day.
              </p></div>
            </details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- Photographs of real jobs. Generated by
       tools/gallery/add-photo-strips.ps1 -- edit the mapping there, not
       here, or the next run will not know this strip exists. -->
  <section class="section is-tight on-sunk" aria-labelledby="shots-service-intercity-relocation" data-photo-strip>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">From our own jobs</span>
        <h2 id="shots-service-intercity-relocation">Packed for the distance</h2>
        <p class="lead">Long-distance consignments get the same sheeting and the same edge protection, strapped so nothing shifts on the road.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="workshots">
        <figure class="workshot">
          <img class="workshot__img"
               src="/assets/images/gallery/packed-items-beside-vehicle-400.jpg"
